3. EVENTRA MANAGE — EVENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

This is the foundation for the entire platform.

Develop a comprehensive event management experience.

3.1 Event creation

Allow authenticated organisers to create events.

Provide the following event information:

* Event title.
* Event description.
* Event category.
* Event cover image.
* Event date.
* Start time.
* End time.
* Time zone.
* Venue name.
* Full event address.
* City.
* Country.
* Online or physical event.
* Online meeting URL where applicable.
* Organiser name.
* Organiser contact information.
* Event website where available.

Support event categories such as:

* Business.
* Conferences.
* Workshops.
* Education.
* Technology.
* Religion and Faith.
* Church Events.
* Music.
* Entertainment.
* Networking.
* Community.
* Charity.
* Health and Wellness.
* Sports.
* Lifestyle.
* Weddings and Celebrations.
* Other.

Organisers should be able to select the most appropriate category.

3.2 Event visibility

Introduce event visibility settings.

Every event must have one of the following visibility states:

Public

The event can appear on Eventra Discover and be accessed by anyone through its public event page.

Unlisted

The event does not appear in public discovery but can be accessed by people who have the sharing link.

Private

The event is restricted to authorised organisers and invited participants through appropriate access controls.

The default should be Public for organisers creating an event intended for discovery, but the organiser must explicitly be able to change it.

Do not confuse event publication status with event visibility.

An event should have separate fields for:

* Publication status.
* Visibility.
* Registration status.

3.3 Event statuses

Support:

* Draft.
* Published.
* Completed.
* Cancelled.
* Archived.

Prevent cancelled or unpublished events from appearing as active public recommendations.

3.4 Event editing

Organisers must be able to:

* Edit event details.
* Change the event image.
* Change the date and time.
* Update location.
* Change visibility.
* Update registration settings.
* Publish or unpublish an event.
* Cancel an event.
* Archive an event.

Provide confirmation dialogs for important destructive actions.

3.5 Event management dashboard

Create an individual management workspace for each event.

Each event workspace should include:

* Event overview.
* Event details.
* Public event page link.
* Invitation management.
* Registration management.
* Attendee list.
* Eventra Create access.
