14. SUPABASE SECURITY AND PRIVACY

Security is essential because Eventra will handle personal information.

Implement appropriate Row Level Security policies.

Organisers

Organisers should only manage events they own or have permission to manage through their organisation.

Attendees

Attendees should only access their own account-based registrations, saved events and personal information.

Public visitors

Public visitors should only access published public event information.

Unlisted events must not appear in public discovery.

Private events must remain private.

Registration submissions

Public registration submissions should be processed through secure operations.

Do not grant unrestricted anonymous SELECT access to event registrations.

Do not allow participants to view other participants’ personal information.

Invitation links

Use unique, high-entropy invitation tokens.

Do not expose sequential database IDs.

Validate invitation access and response permissions.

Organiser permissions

Every event-management action must verify ownership or authorised organisation membership.

Data handling

* Never expose service-role keys.
* Validate user input.
* Validate uploads.
* Apply file-size limits.
* Use signed URLs where appropriate.
* Avoid unnecessary personal data collection.
* Provide appropriate deletion and retention mechanisms.
* Protect against duplicate registration submissions.
* Rate-limit public forms.

Implement privacy-conscious analytics and avoid unnecessary tracking cookies.

